# Translation of ryoku/shell/systemd/user/ryoku-session.target.
# runit has no targets: the session is the roster of services below plus the
# order the session wrapper starts them in. One service per line; '#' comments
# ignored. The wrapper (future work, see void/README.md) reads this file to
# bring the session up, and `sv up`/`sv down` on individual entries replaces
# `systemctl --user start/stop`.
#
# Order mirrors the systemd graph: bootstrap first (config must exist before
# the compositor reads it), then the wallpaper and shell daemons, then the
# policy daemons that hang off the session.
# ryoku-eq is deliberately absent: like its systemd original (no [Install]),
# it is started on demand by the ryoku-eq tool. ryoku-prowl is absent for the
# same reason its unit has no [Install]: ryoku-rashin's run/finish bring it up
# and down (the BindsTo translation).
ryoku-bootstrap
ryogami
ryoku-shell
ryoku-idle
ryoku-clamshell
ryoku-ai-usage
ryoku-bt-agent
ryoku-palette-bridge
ryoku-rashin
ryoku-bluetooth-reset
